          },
          {
            "n": "3.",
            "prompt": "1. I want to be a juror in the house, but my son does not allow me to be a\njuror here.   δικάσαι δικάζειν"
          },
          {
            "n": "2.",
            "prompt": "We must all go out into the market-place.   ἐξιέναι"
          },
          {
            "n": "3.",
            "prompt": "What must you do?   ποιῆσαι"
          },
          {
            "n": "4.",
            "prompt": "It is permissible for Philokleon to prosecute.   κατηγορεῖν"
          },
          {
            "n": "5.",
            "prompt": "The son did not allow his father to go out to the lawcourt.   ἐλθεῖν"
          },
          {
            "n": "6.",
            "prompt": "How shall I persuade you, father, to listen to all the\nspeeches?   ἀκοῦσαι"
          },
          {
            "n": "7.",
            "prompt": "Why aren't you willing to bring out Philokleon, mule?\nἐξενεγκεῖν"
          },
          {
            "n": "8.",
            "prompt": "You (s.) must become a juror in the house.   γενέσθαι"
          },
          {
            "n": "9.",
            "prompt": "They must learn the words of the play.   μαθεῖν"
          },
          {
            "n": "10.",
            "prompt": "He himself wants to keep taking the whole fee from his\nson.   λαμβάνειν"
          },
          {
            "n": "11.",
            "prompt": "I shall not allow him to reach the lawcourt.   ἀφικνεῖσθαι"
          },
          {
            "n": "12.",
            "prompt": "It is possible for me both to take the whole reward here and eat\nit.   λαβεῖν, φαγεῖν"
          }
        ]
      },
